    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. Here is the quantum trick that sounds like a contradiction: two qubits can form one perfectly known pure state while either qubit alone is pure noise.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "How can a pure Bell pair have maximally mixed parts?",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — ENTANGLEMENT",
            "segment": "A Certain Whole, Noisy Parts",
            "greeting": "Bonjour, Liam",
            "runningText": "tracing out one qubit…",
            "output": [
              "The joint state has purity one.",
              "Each local state is I/2."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.13,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Start with the Bell state phi plus: zero-zero plus one-one, with equal amplitudes. There is one exact joint vector, not a classical fifty-fifty lottery between two product states.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "drawon"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.71,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "The whole pair is pure. Its density operator is a rank-one projector, and its purity — trace of rho squared — equals one.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 7.38,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "Now lock Bob's qubit in a box and ask every possible question about Alice's qubit alone. What state predicts all of those local measurements?",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.66,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "narration_text": "The partial trace discards Bob from the description. It is bookkeeping, not a physical measurement. The cross terms vanish because zero and one are orthogonal, leaving one half zero-zero plus one half one-one.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.99,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "That reduced state is identity over two. Alice's Bloch vector sits at the center, and her local purity is one half — the smallest possible value for a qubit.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.51,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Measure Alice along z, x, y, or any other axis. Each binary outcome is locally fifty-fifty. No direction reveals a hidden arrow, because her reduced Bloch vector is zero.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "scan"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.07,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "But bring Bob's records back and the structure reappears. In the z basis, their outcomes always match. The information was never in Alice or Bob separately; it was in the relationship.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.52,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "narration_text": "Do not overstate that as same answer on every axis. For phi plus, correlations depend on the chosen axes: same along z and x, opposite along y. Local randomness is universal; the joint pattern is state and basis dependent.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.72,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Compare a product state, zero-zero. The whole is pure and Alice is also pure: her arrow points north. Pure parts are possible only when the pure joint state is not entangled.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.39,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "So entanglement does not add ordinary uncertainty to a hidden local state. It moves the complete description into correlations that no state vector for either part can carry.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.5,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "And tracing out Bob does not claim Bob vanished or was measured. It constructs the unique local density matrix that gets every Alice-only experiment right.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "hold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B12.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.54,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B12.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B13",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "The verdict: the Bell pair is perfectly definite globally and maximally mixed locally. The apparent paradox disappears once you stop demanding that information live inside one object. Here, it lives between two.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B13.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.39,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B13.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:24:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B14",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. Paste this into Claude: Compare the reduced states and measurement correlations of phi plus and the product state zero-zero in the z, x, and y bases. Ask it to separate local statistics from joint statistics. That separation is the whole lesson.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Compare the reduced states and measurement correlations of |Phi+> and |00> in the z, x, and y bases. Separate local from joint statistics.",
            "topic": "YOUR TURN",
            "segment": "Find Where the Information Lives",
            "greeting": "Your turn.",
            "runningText": "paste this into Claude…",
            "output": [
              "First compute each reduced state.",
              "Then compare the correlation signs."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
